AI UPSCALE AND PROCESSING
The separately delivered 6144x4096 master uses genuine 4x inference with the official Real-ESRGAN x4plus anime 6B model through NCNN CPU. The 3072x2048 option is that master reduced with Pillow Lanczos, not a native 2x model. Upscaling does not recover unavailable ground-truth detail.
A continuous source is processed as 70 computational tiles with 160px cores, 32px context and 16px additional reflected processing border. The context is discarded without blending and all inferred core pixels assembled into one canvas. This is computational tiling, not artistic stitching. Each tile uses an isolated child process. The script requests 2 threads after loading; the NCNN load-time thread setting is 4. OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 is also set.
Completed inference wall time for this scene: 238.563 seconds. Peak child RSS: 3316848 KiB. Actual run records are included under metrics. Two independent untiled sample checks assess tile-boundary consistency; results retain all observed differences in metrics/seam_metrics.json. They are neither exhaustive seam certification nor high-resolution ground-truth validation.

HERO-SCALE REVIEWS
The supplied original RGBA hero is alpha-cropped at alpha > 30 and conventionally resized with Lanczos to 160px visible height, then composited with a small grounding shadow. The art uses a 64px source-equivalent hero, or 256px in raw 4x. Raw 4x scenery is reduced by 0.625 to 3840x2560, corresponding to 2.5x native art display. Each 1536x1024 review viewport therefore covers 614.4x409.6 native pixels. Crop boxes and foot locations are in review_config.json and review_views_metadata.json.
Three distinct viewports and their overview were visually inspected. Hero feet sit on apparently clear ground and the complete hero stays inside each crop. Hero/shadow overlays exist only in review previews, never in native or upscaled fullscenes. Engine scale, collision, navigation, height transitions and occlusion remain unvalidated.

